course: dictionary
lesson: 2110
title: One word, many meanings: control
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word control can mean different things, so the words around it tell you which meaning to use. «A factory robot is controlled by a computer that drives motors in each joint.» Here control means to make a machine do what you want, like steering a toy car.
explain: Control can also be about feelings and power over people. «Someone who tells you who you can't be friends with is controlling, not being a friend.» The sentence shows that controlling someone is not kind, because it takes away their choices.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If control means make something do what you want, does the sentence still make sense? If it does not, try another meaning, such as keep calm or have power over.
fact: Control can be a verb (to control something) or a noun (the control, or being in control).
fact: To control yourself means to keep calm and not let anger or tears take over.
fact: «Out of control» means nobody can stop it, and «under control» means it is safe and steady.
fact: In a science experiment, the control is the part you keep the same so you can compare.
fact: «Controls» are the buttons, levers or knobs that work a machine, like a remote control for the TV.
exercise: «A factory robot is controlled by a computer.» What does controlled mean here? | Left alone to rest | *Made to do what the computer tells it | Taken apart for spare parts | Painted bright colours
exercise: In a science test, what is the control? | The scientist who writes the report | The part you change on purpose | *The part you keep the same so you can compare | The results written at the end
exercise: Sam says, «I need to control my temper.» What does control mean here? | Shout as loudly as he can | Make his temper disappear for ever | Buy a new temper from the shop | *Keep calm and not let anger take over
test: «Someone who tells you who you can't be friends with is controlling, not being a friend.» What does controlling mean here? | Making lots of new friends | Being late for school | Being very kind to everybody | *Trying to have power over someone's choices
test: The car was out of control on the icy road. What does out of control mean? | *Nobody could stop it | Parked safely in the garage | Full of fuel and ready to go | Driving slowly under a bridge
exam: «Apes cannot speak words like us because their throat, tongue and breathing control are different.» What does control mean here? | *The ability to move and use their throat, tongue and breath on purpose | A cage that keeps them safe | Snacks they are allowed to eat | Sounds that come out by accident
